// The hand cases of rule (c) part 2: in each, `leak` frees an object whose inner owner holds an
// allocation, and `free` or `twice` frees one whose inner owners are empty. In `local` a store into
// an inner owner of a fresh pointer kills its fact, and a `del` of the owner gives it again. In
// `param` the parameter has no fact at the entry. In `memory` the address of the pointer makes it
// memory, so no place through it is tracked, and the `del` of `free` is a false reject. In `call`
// a call kills each fact through the pointer, reached through memory, so `twice`, which frees one
// owner after the call, is a false reject. In `cast` the obligation stands at a `cast` to `void*
// own`, and the run leaks at the `del` of its result, which the event marks at the `cast` of its
// function. In `span` the elements of a span hold the owners, which wait for refinement R8 (Q7),
// so the case has no site and one leak of a span. In `nested` the inner owners lie in a nested
// struct and in a fixed array, whose elements have constant keys: a store into `kids[1]` kills the
// facts of both elements, and `leak` gives back only that of `kids[0]`. In `twin` a deferred `del`
// expands at two exits with one location, and in `abort` the `del` before a `panic` keeps its
// obligation (D17.20 gives part 2 no exception for an abort block). In `field` the `del` of a field
// is a site that the pass cannot prove, and `free` takes the fix of D17.20: it moves the inner
// owner into a local first. In `owner` the object of the pointer is itself the inner owner. In
// `tested` the `del` in the arm where the test finds null frees nothing, and the `del` of the other
// arm leaks. In `tested_field` the loop on `l->head != null` leaves the field empty at its end, so
// its `del` frees nothing, and the `del` of the field in `leak` leaks. Its places name no place
// that the loop tests: a store into such a place at the end of the loop body would never end the
// loop. The seeded family inserts into these cases too.
// The count of the lines of DEL_CASES.
u64 DEL_LINES = 333;

