// The hand cases of rule (b) of D17.21, each a program that the shadow interpreter runs. In
// `deleted`, `moved`, `field`, `element`, `borrowed`, `span`, `struct_move` and `nested` a load
// reads an owner after a `del` or a `move` of a place that can overlap it, and in `copied` a copy
// of the vacated owner is the use and the load reads through the copy. In `callee` a call deletes
// the owner through its address, and the load after the call reads the vacated owner; in
// `call_memory` the call deletes nothing, and the rule still takes the memory owner as vacated. In
// `looped` the second pass of the loop reads the owner that the `del` of the first pass vacated.
// `key_store` is the example of D17.21 with two keys, `deferred` reads the owner in a deferred
// block after its `del`, `argument` is `take(move(p), *p)`, `ternary` reads the owner in an arm
// of `?:` after a `del` in an arm of an `if`, and `null_edge` loads through the owner on the edge
// where its test finds null, which ends no state. `global_ptr` loads through a global that holds
// the address of the owner, with no call. `tested`, `refilled`, `null_arm`, `refill_loop`,
// `and_guard` and `while_test` keep the rule: a test against null guards the load, or a store
// fills the owner again. The seeded family inserts into these cases too. The places of
// `while_test` name `y` and not the owner that its loop tests, and its loop ends at its `del` or
// at its `break`: a variant inserts or removes one statement, and a store into the tested owner,
// or a removed `del` with no `break`, would never end the loop.
// The count of the lines of USE_CASES.
u64 USE_LINES = 283;

